      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "This change is tedious to review, but I think worth it. Having tests that use mutable structs over hundreds of lines and separate unit test cases and each case may modify some fields of the struct leads to test bugs (copy-paste errors) and makes it harder to read the test, because more time is spent on trying to figure out the current state than the test logic itself.\n\nSo rough Concept ACK, but obviously the approach may differ on a case-by-case basis. ",
