      "body": "> **declarative construction**:\n> \n> const CTransaction tx_1{\n>     std::array{\n>         CTxIn{...}...\n\n\nbtw, I am not sure on forcing the call sites to specify a container. This is verbose and distracting in test code. If this is done, the ctor should simply accept a `std::vector<T> vin/out`. This keeps all call sites clean and possibly also avoids a copy on the stack (not that performance is relevant here)? Of course, fancy callers can still do fancy stuff like passing `(std::views::concat(a, b) | std::ranges::to<std::vector>());`, but then the fancy stuff only requires verbose code at the fancy call sites. So my preference would be to keep this plain and simple C++11.",
