      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Right, but I'd still prefer the plain and less verbose C++11 ctor here. Recall the goal is to mostly catch accidental bugs in tests, not intentional bugs. If we are worried about the mutable reference backdoor, I think it can be trivially fixed in C++11 by just doing the copy (performance doesn't matter for this test-only code). While clang-tidy use-after-free doesn't catch such partial moves, I am sure human or LLM reviewers will catch it, so I wouldn't worry too much about it.",
